1
00:00:03,051 --> 00:00:05,205
At the museum, a giant skeleton!

2
00:00:05,255 --> 00:00:08,579
Dinosaurs disappeared a very, very long time ago.

3
00:00:08,629 --> 00:00:10,764
So how do we know they existed?

4
00:00:11,552 --> 00:00:13,745
These bones are not real bones:

5
00:00:13,795 --> 00:00:15,409
they turned into stone.

6
00:00:15,459 --> 00:00:15,988
Fossils!

7
00:00:16,038 --> 00:00:18,281
Mila finds them cold and heavy.

8
00:00:19,062 --> 00:00:20,576
Discovery mission!

9
00:00:23,092 --> 00:00:23,751
Mini mode!

10
00:00:23,801 --> 00:00:25,807
A dinosaur dies near a river.

11
00:00:25,857 --> 00:00:28,572
Its skin and muscles disappear quickly.

12
00:00:28,622 --> 00:00:30,983
Then sand and mud cover its bones,

13
00:00:31,033 --> 00:00:32,309
layer after layer.

14
00:00:33,090 --> 00:00:36,926
Underground, water seeps into the bones and leaves minerals behind:

15
00:00:36,976 --> 00:00:39,363
the bone turns to stone, little by little.

16
00:00:39,413 --> 00:00:41,791
Above, the layers get squashed into rock.

17
00:00:42,572 --> 00:00:43,983
Millions of years later,

18
00:00:44,033 --> 00:00:46,601
the rock wears away and the fossil appears.

19
00:00:46,651 --> 00:00:47,088
Its age?

20
00:00:47,138 --> 00:00:49,462
The volcanic ash around it has a clock:

21
00:00:49,512 --> 00:00:51,642
atoms that change at a known speed.

22
00:00:52,434 --> 00:00:54,326
Bones, teeth, footprints, eggs:

23
00:00:54,376 --> 00:00:56,707
thousands of fossils around the world.

24
00:00:56,757 --> 00:00:58,649
Becoming a fossil is very rare…

25
00:00:58,699 --> 00:01:01,268
but over millions of years, that adds up!

26
00:01:02,052 --> 00:01:04,707
That's how we know dinosaurs existed.

27
00:01:05,554 --> 00:01:07,515
Dinosaur bones turned to stone:

28
00:01:07,565 --> 00:01:10,030
fossils are the proof that they lived.

29
00:01:11,068 --> 00:01:15,078
With an adult: press a shell or a toy into modelling clay,

30
00:01:15,128 --> 00:01:16,268
then lift it off.

31
00:01:16,318 --> 00:01:18,628
Your print is a miniature fossil!

32
00:01:19,432 --> 00:01:20,931
And where does the wind come from?

33
00:01:20,981 --> 00:01:21,892
The answer tomorrow.
